# Testing Rules

## Test Organization

- Unit tests: co-located with source files as `*.spec.ts`
- E2E tests: placed in `test/` directory with `*.e2e-spec.ts`
- Test utilities: placed in `test/packages/` directory

## Unit Test Patterns

```typescript
describe('{ClassName}', () => {
  let service: {Name}Service;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [
        {Name}Service,
        { provide: '{Name}Repository', useValue: mockRepository },
      ],
    }).compile();

    service = module.get({Name}Service);
  });

  describe('create', () => {
    it('should create a new record', async () => {
      const dto: CreateDto = { /* ... */ };
      const result = await service.create(dto);
      expect(result).toBeDefined();
      expect(result.id).toBeDefined();
    });
  });
});
```

## Mocking Rules

- Mock external dependencies (DB, Redis, email) in unit tests
- Use `jest.fn()` or `jest.spyOn()` for mocking
- Never call real databases in unit tests
- Reset all mocks in `afterEach` or `beforeEach`

## Coverage Requirements

- Minimum coverage thresholds (configured in jest config)
  - Branches: 80%
  - Functions: 85%
  - Lines: 85%
  - Statements: 85%
- Focus on service layer testing
- Controller tests should validate decorators and pipes

## E2E Test Patterns

```typescript
describe('{Feature} (e2e)', () => {
  let app: INestApplication;

  beforeAll(async () => {
    const moduleFixture = await Test.createTestingModule({
      imports: [AppModule],
    }).compile();

    app = moduleFixture.createNestApplication();
    await app.init();
  });

  describe('POST /{path}', () => {
    it('should return 201 on success', () => {
      return request(app.getHttpServer())
        .post('/{path}')
        .send({
          /* dto */
        })
        .expect(201);
    });
  });
});
```

## Test Naming Convention

- Describe blocks: `describe('methodName', () => { ... })`
- It blocks: `it('should [expected behavior] when [condition]', () => { ... })`
- Use `given/when/then` comments for complex test cases
